+> **Description:** AutoGen is Microsoft’s framework for building multi-agent AI applications that can act autonomously or collaborate with humans. The README highlights assistant agents, tool use, MCP support, console and studio interfaces, and coordination patterns for expert agents working together on tasks. It is especially useful when you want explicit agent-to-agent interaction rather than a single chain or chat wrapper. GitHub shows a very large Python-led codebase with dual licensing visible in the repository, strong community traction, and ongoing development activity that keeps it relevant for agentic application development in 2026.
