+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for LLM development in 2026?
+The strongest open source starting points depend on the layer you need. For orchestration, `LangChain`, `LangGraph`, `AutoGen`, `CrewAI`, and `LlamaIndex` lead the field. For self-hosted product stacks, `Dify`, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, `Open WebUI`, and `AnythingLLM` are the most practical. For runtime and serving, `Ollama`, `vLLM`, `llama.cpp`, `Text Generation Inference`, and `LocalAI` cover most local and production needs.
+
+### Which GitHub tools are best for self-hosted LLM app development?
+`Dify`, `Open WebUI`, `AnythingLLM`, `Flowise`, and `Langflow` are the strongest self-hosted app-layer choices in this list. They help you ship internal copilots, knowledge assistants, and workflow-driven AI apps without relying on proprietary SaaS-only products.
+
+### What is the best open source stack for RAG and retrieval in 2026?
+For RAG-heavy systems, a common open source stack is `LlamaIndex` or `Haystack` for application logic, `Qdrant`, `Weaviate`, `Milvus`, or `Chroma` for vector retrieval, and `Langfuse`, `Phoenix`, or `Ragas` for visibility and evaluation. The right choice depends on whether you optimize for scale, speed, or developer simplicity.
+
+### Which open source tools help test prompts and evaluate LLM apps?
+`promptfoo`, `Ragas`, `DeepEval`, `Langfuse`, and `Phoenix` are the most evaluation-oriented tools in this repository. They cover prompt regression checks, RAG metrics, traces, experimentation, output scoring, and release gating workflows.
+
+### What is the best local runtime for open models on a laptop?
+`Ollama` and `llama.cpp` are the best-known laptop-friendly choices. `Ollama` wins on ease of use and packaging, while `llama.cpp` offers deeper low-level control and excellent support for quantized models on commodity hardware.
+
+### Are these AI tools really open source and GitHub-only?
+Yes. This repository only includes tools that have a public `github.com` URL and excludes proprietary SaaS-only products. Some projects have unusual or mixed licenses, so the GitHub-declared license is listed for every entry and should be reviewed before production use.
