+> **Description:** LangChain positions itself as an agent engineering platform for building applications around large language models. The project README focuses on composable chains, tool calling, retrieval workflows, structured outputs, memory patterns, and model integrations across major providers. It is widely used for production RAG systems and agent prototypes because it gives developers abstractions for prompts, models, retrievers, callbacks, and runtime orchestration in one ecosystem. GitHub metadata at verification time shows a large Python codebase under the MIT License with very active maintenance, broad community adoption, and frequent upstream changes across integrations and agent tooling.
